  "mood": "hazy and hushed",
  "summary": "the day ends with fishmongers selling their last haul of scraps before the fog settles over the harbour, leaving only silence and salt",
  "details": "the air smells of brine and dust, and the stalls are packed tight. a man trades a worn coat for fresh catfish scraps while shouting loudly to fill the quiet air, and children pick over discarded jars of preserved fruit, their hands stained brown from the work. it is a quiet place where time moves slowly and all things are worth their price."
